A||||13||gt2437||Frame flex -- who's got it ?  :)||||11||
Z||000000||gt2437||07-13-2001||03:33 PM||||So who has frame flex??  I have quite a bit.  I know the car was in an accident before I got it, which definitely plays a role.  Both my B pillars creak and groan and the drivers side roof, in front of the sunroof by the A pillar, actually clicks.  <P>The car is lowered, but it had this problem before the suspension was swapped out.   My project GT is very solid and I'm going to put drop spindles and coilovers on it to keep it tight. (Well tighter than lowering springs).  Any comments from stock suspended and lowered fiero owners would be greatly appreciated  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Go to <A HREF="http://www.mumz.org" TARGET=_blank>http://www.mumz.org</A>  for a pic of my car (or sig).<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/ViewPhoto?u=1486717&a=11524521&p=47383883&f=0" TARGET=_blank>1986 Pontiac Fiero GT</A><BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumIndex?u=1486717&a=11204369&f=0" TARGET=_blank>2000 VW 1.8T NB</A>||||reg||11
Z||000001||DecadenceR||07-13-2001||04:03 PM||||When I'm making a turn into a store parking lot and I have the sunroof open, I can hear the creaking. BUt I know i'm safe. i already wrecked one...||||reg||1
