Z||000005||fiero56||07-13-2001||05:22 PM||||I get wind noise through my sunroof, but my Fiero('88) has never made noises as I go over curbs, or any other frame-tensioning surface. It's got 177K on it right now. Maybe previous years are a little different?||||reg||1
Z||000006||Hartz||07-13-2001||05:37 PM||||My car makes all kind of noise going over curbs, up steep driveways, etc.  But then again, with the suspension work I've done, it will also lift a front wheel off the ground doing that, so I don't think there's that much flex going on!<P>Hartz<BR>'84 SC 5.7L V8<BR>'85 SE 3.1L V6 Turbo||||reg||1
Z||000007||gt2437||07-13-2001||09:53 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fiero56:<BR><B>I get wind noise through my sunroof, but my Fiero('88) has never made noises as I go over curbs, or any other frame-tensioning surface. It's got 177K on it right now. Maybe previous years are a little different?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Alex4mula has an '88 as well  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  Glad to hear yours is quite solid.  My sunroof has warped and does not seal by the latch (sits up 3/16"), most likely due to age alone.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Hartz:<BR><B>My car makes all kind of noise going over curbs, up steep driveways, etc. But then again, with the suspension work I've done, it will also lift a front wheel off the ground doing that, so I don't think there's that much flex going on!?<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  hahaha very nice<P>||||reg||14
Z||000008||PBJ||07-13-2001||10:11 PM||||I would say all these noises and creaks are pretty normal with a metal frame covered with plastics and fiber glass clipped to it.  <P>There is quite a few service bulletins from GM in regards to body creaks, especially from roof area.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000009||artherd||07-13-2001||11:01 PM||||My Formulas are both totally solid (even the t-top one!!)<P>The only part of the cars that do anything but work are the doors. The damn things feel like they have a life (or at least a dozen resonance modes) of their own!!!<P>Someday when I get around to it, I will redo them in Carbonfibre (have to keep the same lfvel of side-impact protection the current ones offer though, so it is not a trivial engineering project, as carbonfibre's stregenths are largely in one dimention for a single sheeting layup method.)<P>Best!<BR>Ben<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000010||Alex2004||07-14-2001||12:00 AM||||The only time i've noticed mine creaking was wheni went up a hill at an angle going sorta fast or like today when i went through the drive through at a restaurant here in town and i had to go down in an angle so i wouldn't scrape and the drivers front wheel came off the ground (IT WAS STEEP), mine has a sunroof too and is stil pretty solid.<P>Alex...||||reg||1
Z||000011||Mach10||07-14-2001||12:21 PM||||I can pick up both tires when lifting from the frame in the back  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>I love having a cherry frame  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>My sunroof creaks when I hit a large bump. That's it.||||reg||6
